        "example": "A grading panel auditing whether an examiner simply awards higher essays to whoever fills three pages instead of checking insight.",
        "code": "def audit_verbosity_bias(records):\n    long_wins = 0\n    asym_cases = 0\n    for r in records:\n        longer_winner = (r[\"len_a\"] > r[\"len_b\"] * 1.5 and r[\"win\"] == \"A\") or (r[\"len_b\"] > r[\"len_a\"] * 1.5 and r[\"win\"] == \"B\")\n        asym = (r[\"len_a\"] > r[\"len_b\"] * 1.5) or (r[\"len_b\"] > r[\"len_a\"] * 1.5)\n        if asym:\n            asym_cases += 1\n            if longer_winner:\n                long_wins += 1\n    pct = round(long_wins / asym_cases * 100, 1) if asym_cases else 0.0\n    return {\"asym_cases\": asym_cases, \"longer_win_pct\": pct, \"verbosity_warning\": pct > 75.0}\n\nsample = [\n    {\"len_a\": 200, \"len_b\": 60, \"win\": \"A\"},\n    {\"len_a\": 50,  \"len_b\": 190, \"win\": \"B\"},\n    {\"len_a\": 220, \"len_b\": 70, \"win\": \"A\"},\n    {\"len_a\": 180, \"len_b\": 55, \"win\": \"B\"},\n]\nprint(audit_verbosity_bias(sample))",
